§ `Part VIA - Residential tenancy databases`

§§ `Division 2 - Tenancy database information`

§§§ `82E. Listing can be made only for particular breaches by particular persons`

DECLARE `proposed listing` HAS
    `the person was named as a tenant in a residential tenancy agreement that has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has breached the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the breach consists of or relates to a failure to pay rent during the COVID-19 emergency period due to financial hardship caused by the economic effects of the COVID-19 pandemic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the breach consists of or relates to any other matter relating to the effects of the COVID-19 pandemic prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `because of the breach the person owes the lessor an amount that is more than the security bond for the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `because of the breach a court has made an order terminating the residential tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.82E
@export Decide whether personal information about a person may be listed in a residential tenancy database under s.82E
GIVEN l IS A `proposed listing` @desc A lessor, lessor's agent or database operator must not list unless: the person was named as a tenant in an ended agreement; the person breached it; the breach is not a prescribed COVID-19 rent-hardship or other prescribed COVID-19 matter; and because of the breach the person owes more than the security bond or a court has terminated the agreement.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the listing of personal information is permitted` IF
        l's `the person was named as a tenant in a residential tenancy agreement that has ended`
    AND l's `the person has breached the agreement`
    AND NOT l's `the breach consists of or relates to a failure to pay rent during the COVID-19 emergency period due to financial hardship caused by the economic effects of the COVID-19 pandemic`
    AND NOT l's `the breach consists of or relates to any other matter relating to the effects of the COVID-19 pandemic prescribed by regulations`
    AND (
            l's `because of the breach the person owes the lessor an amount that is more than the security bond for the agreement`
        OR  l's `because of the breach a court has made an order terminating the residential tenancy agreement`
        )

§§ `Fixtures`

`bond exceeded after ended tenancy` MEANS `proposed listing` WITH
    `the person was named as a tenant in a residential tenancy agreement that has ended` IS TRUE,
    `the person has breached the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the breach consists of or relates to a failure to pay rent during the COVID-19 emergency period due to financial hardship caused by the economic effects of the COVID-19 pandemic` IS FALSE,
    `the breach consists of or relates to any other matter relating to the effects of the COVID-19 pandemic prescribed by regulations` IS FALSE,
    `because of the breach the person owes the lessor an amount that is more than the security bond for the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `because of the breach a court has made an order terminating the residential tenancy agreement` IS FALSE

`covid rent hardship listing` MEANS `proposed listing` WITH
    `the person was named as a tenant in a residential tenancy agreement that has ended` IS TRUE,
    `the person has breached the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the breach consists of or relates to a failure to pay rent during the COVID-19 emergency period due to financial hardship caused by the economic effects of the COVID-19 pandemic` IS TRUE,
    `the breach consists of or relates to any other matter relating to the effects of the COVID-19 pandemic prescribed by regulations` IS FALSE,
    `because of the breach the person owes the lessor an amount that is more than the security bond for the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `because of the breach a court has made an order terminating the residential tenancy agreement` IS FALSE

#EVAL `the listing of personal information is permitted` `bond exceeded after ended tenancy`
#EVAL `the listing of personal information is permitted` `covid rent hardship listing`
#ASSERT `the listing of personal information is permitted` `bond exceeded after ended tenancy` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the listing of personal information is permitted` `covid rent hardship listing` EQUALS FALSE
